# Dexicon — .gitignore
#
# SECRETS MODEL (docs/10-security-secrets.md): secrets are NEVER committed.
# `.env.example` is the only tracked template; every real value lives in `.env`,
# `secrets/`, or the environment. This file exists from the first commit because
# secret hygiene retrofitted before a public push has already failed — the
# history is what gets scanned.

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.local.json
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.local.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.pem

# ── Runtime data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Catalogue, uploaded blobs, local volumes. Never reconstructible, never committed.
data/
.dexicon/
workspaces/

# ── .NET ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
publish/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage/

# ── Node / SPA ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
.eslintcache

# ── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tmp/
*.tmp
*.log

# ── SPA build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfile builds clients/web-ui and copies dist/ into wwwroot. Committing
# the built bundle means shipping whatever was on someone's laptop, and it goes
# stale the moment the source changes.
#
# The WHOLE directory is ignored, not just assets/: `dev.ps1 ui` copies dist/*,
# which includes index.html, so a tracked placeholder there was silently
# clobbered and re-committed on every UI build. The server serves an explanatory
# page from code when the directory is empty, which is the same outcome without
# a file that fights the build.
src/Dexicon/wwwroot/*
!src/Dexicon/wwwroot/.gitkeep

# Generated from Dexicon.json by `npm run generate`. Reproducible from the OpenAPI
# document, which IS tracked — so the diff that matters (the contract) is reviewable
# without 1,000 lines of generated TypeScript in every pull request.
clients/web-ui/src/generated/

# The benchmark harness (scripts/bench) is Python. Without these, running a sweep
# leaves a compiled sweep.cpython-314.pyc in the tree — and one of them was committed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
